T*
(In an age that rewards speed, slow reading can seem almost subversive.) Tj T*
(We skim headlines, scroll past paragraphs and mistake familiarity for) Tj T*
(understanding. Much as I sympathise with the view that time is scarce,) Tj T*
(I would argue that reading quickly often means reading nothing at all.) Tj T*
T*
(Slow reading is not merely reading at a lower speed. It is a deliberate) Tj T*
(practice of noticing: the choice of a verb, the rhythm of a clause, the) Tj T*
(way a writer concedes a point before overturning it.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
