T*
(Advanced learners rarely lack vocabulary in the narrow sense. What they) Tj T*
(lack is a feel for collocation and nuance. A careful reader notices that) Tj T*
(evidence is compelling rather than strong, and that a problem is tackled) Tj T*
(rather than fixed. Such details are seldom taught, yet they are precisely) Tj T*
(what distinguishes fluent writing from merely correct writing.) Tj T*
T*
(Not only does slow reading sharpen comprehension, but it also builds a) Tj T*
(private store of phrases that can later be borrowed and adapted.) Tj T*
